OL,3,AThames Water apologises after #145,000
OL,4,Acustomer billing mistake
OL,5,
OL,6,FThames Water has apologised to a
OL,7,Fcustomer after trying to take #145,000
OL,8,Ffrom his bank account due to a meter
OL,9,Freading error by the company.
OL,11,FAdam Bainbridge, a teacher from north
OL,12,FLondon, discovered while routinely
OL,13,Fchecking his accounts on Thursday
OL,14,Fmorning that Thames had debited
OL,15,F#145,562 from his bank account.
OL,17,FHis wife Julia told the PA news agency
OL,18,Fthat Adam "got the shock of his life"
OL,19,Fand had trouble paying bills that
OL,20,Fmorning as a result.
OL,23,APub: 01-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
FL,114,105,200,300,0,100
